##Just Rich — Privacy Policy

Last update: October 22, 2026.

This policy describes the operation of the iPhone application "Just Rich" and the exchanges with its support.

Contact

For any questions regarding this policy or your data, contact the application developer:

##Justracedstudio@gmail.com

Data stored on your iPhone

The application locally records the first name entered, the chosen address formula, the notification preferences and the information necessary for its operation, including the sentences displayed, the stories of the day and the history avoiding repetitions.

This information allows you to keep your profile, customize the address formula, schedule reminders and find the phrases of the day. They are not sent by the application to the developer or to an external server.

The application does not ask for an account. It does not include advertising, audience analysis tools, or advertising tracking. It does not access your contacts, photos, location or financial data. It does not check your assets.

Notifications

Notifications are optional and subject to your permission in iOS. They are programmed and presented locally by the system, without the developer's notification server. Their text can include your custom address formula and appear on the locked screen according to your iOS settings.

You can change their frequency in the app or withdraw permission in iOS notification settings. The application does not observe the iPhone unlocks.

Retention and deletion of local data

The profile and preferences remain saved until they are modified or deleted from the application. Stories are replaced when the application sees a new local day. The monthly history of sentences remains recorded to limit repetitions; it is not a detailed diary of opening hours.

In case of unreadable saved data, a local recovery copy can be kept. The complete deletion of the application, with its data, also deletes these copies. The iOS option to download the application keeps its data and is not equivalent to a complete deletion.

Depending on your settings, iPhone backups may contain application data. A restoration can therefore restore them. These backups are managed by your backup tools and, if applicable, by Apple; the developer does not have access to them.

Exchanges with support

When you voluntarily write to justracedstudio@gmail.com, your email address, message and any attachments are processed to respond to your request and solve the reported problem. The purpose is to assist users, based on the developer's legitimate interest in providing this assistance.

These exchanges go through Gmail, Google's service, and through your own email provider. Their processing and any international transfers are governed by their respective conditions and privacy policies. Messages are not used for advertising or commercial prospecting.

Exchanges are kept during the processing of the request and, after its closure, only as long as follow-up of the same incident or the management of a dispute requires it. You can request their deletion at the contact address; a legal obligation or the defense of rights may justify the retention of only the necessary information.

Do not send unnecessary passwords, bank details or personal information at your request.

Your rights

You can change your profile in the application settings and delete local data by completely deleting the application. The developer cannot remotely view or erase data from your iPhone.

For the data contained in your exchanges with support, you can request, according to the applicable conditions, access, rectification, erasure, limitation of processing or oppose their processing by writing to justracedstudio@gmail.com. You can also send a complaint to the CNIL: https://www.cnil.fr/fr/plaintes.

Separate services

Apple manages the download and, if applicable, the payment of the application on the App Store according to its own rules. The application does not receive your bank details.

Viewing these pages on GitHub is also part of GitHub's operation and privacy policy. This policy does not describe technical data processed independently by Apple, GitHub or your email provider.

Evolution of this policy

This policy will be updated if the operation of the application or data processing changes. The update date appears at the top of the document.
